AB  - Duolite C225 ion exchange resin (a crosslinked polystyrene with sulphonic acid functional groups) in the sodium form can be successfully immobilised in blended cement systems.The formulation which appears acceptable is manufactured from a 9 to 1 blend of Blast Furnace Slag and Ordinary Portland Cement containing H0% ion exchange resin by weight in the form of a slurry.The product has adequate strength for handling and shows little dimensional change with time.Experiments show that above 50Ï waste loading the product becomes unstable and its strength is unacceptably low.Changes in the metal cation have shown little effect on the properties of the product.Increasing the waste loading appears to have little effect on the hydration rate of the product.Preliminary calculations show that a volume reduction factor of H is obtained by taking the active LOMI effluent, removing the activity onto the Duolite C225 and then immobilising in cement.
