TY  - JOUR
ID  - SG-BD512A2BE23A
TI  - Syngas biomethanation: Current state and future perspectives
AU  - Sergio Paniagua
AU  - Raquel Lebrero
AU  - Raúl Muñoz
JO  - Bioresource Technology
PY  - 2022
DO  - 10.1016/j.biortech.2022.127436
AB  - In regions highly dependent on fossil fuels imports, biomethane represents a promising biofuel for the transition to a bio-based circular economy. While biomethane is typically produced via anaerobic digestion and upgrading, biomethanation of the synthesis gas (syngas) derived from the gasification of recalcitrant solid waste has emerged as a promising alternative. This work presents a comprehensive and in-depth analysis of the state-of-the-art and most recent advances in the field, compiling the potential of this technology along with the bottlenecks requiring further research. The key design and operational parameters governing syngas production and biomethanation (e.g. organic feedstock, gasifier design, microbiology, bioreactor configuration, etc.) are critically analysed.
