TI  - Development of biodegradable and biobased multiphase films for single-use containers used in bioprocesses
AU  - Alexis Morinval
JO  - theses.fr (ABES)
PY  - 2023
DO  - 10.70675/ed61686az2d91z4d1azbe1ezc8e51347ebb4
AB  - After a continuous growth of plastics production since the 1950s, it is time to take charge of the environmental aspects related to these indispensable materials with unique properties. This requires taking into account the beginning (resources) and the end (circularity) of their life cycle, especially by using biobased and biodegradable polymers. In this thesis, renewable films are developed and analyzed for applications to packaging used in biotechnologies. Compatibilized multilayer films based on plasticized starch and a polyester have been coextruded and characterized in order to evaluate their properties and their suitability for the targeted field. In this context, starch and a biodegradable polyester were chemically modified to develop thermoreversible Diels-Alder reactions at the interface. These modified polymers allowed to improve the properties, especially mechanical, of these systems. The thiol-Michael click addition and the disulfide bond exchange have also been studied for the future development of dynamic compatibilized systems with possible end-of-life treatments allowing an easier recycling.
