AB  - This technology converted PCBs into a nontoxic biphenyl leaving behind unprocessed waste oil and biphenyl.Several articles discussed issues related to solid waste, hazardous waste and landfill management.Al-Humoud (2002) presented the current solid waste management practices in Kuwait.The results showed a rapid increase in the total amount of municipal solid wastes and significant changes in their composition.Carlos and Luce (2002) reported the waste management scheme, as well as a brief description of adopted technologies, chemical glass composition and updated schedule of CORA (conditioning of radioactive wastes) project.Mersiowsky (2002) demonstrated by landfill simulation assays the long-term behavior of PVC (polyvinyl chloride) products and fate of additives under landfill conditions.Greenman and Cole (2002) reviewed the requirements mandated by the EPA (Environmental Protection Agency) and the NRC (Nuclear Regulatory Commission) with regard to mixed-waste generation, treatment and disposal.Chakraborty and Linninger (2002) introduced the concept of combinatorial process synthesis for development plant-wide recovery and treatment policies for batch manufacturing sites.They also discussed case studies illustrating the systematic and fully automatic waste management procedures.Fleming et al. (2002) reviewed published medical, epidemiologic, and toxicologic literatures, available governmental reports, and studies from developed and less developed nations related to relevant work-forces.Solid waste workers were exposed to significant levels of physical, chemical and biological toxins.
