TI  - Microbial biofilms in groundwater ecosystems
AU  - Clemens Karwautz
JO  - mediaTUM – the media and publications repository of the Technical University Munich (Technical University Munich)
PY  - 2015
AB  - Microbial biofilms control biogeochemical processes and solute fluxes in groundwater, yet respective studies are scarce. The importance of biofilms in ground- and drinking water systems was addressed in this thesis, by investigating attached microbiota on reactive mineral surfaces in an oligotrophic pristine aquifer, massive lithotrophic biofilms formed in a unique iodine spring cavern, as well as attached microbes in active drinking water wells. A comprehensive discussion of subsurface biofilm ecology is provided.
