AB  - The beginnings of the fermentation industries are shrouded in the mists of antiquity.It was known that the Egyptians of the Fourth Dynasty brewed beer, a venerable age for any industry.But now, thanks to the investigations of E. Huber,1 it has been found that the Egyptians learnt the art from the peoples of the valleys of the Tigris and Euphrates, that beer already played an important part in domestic economy as long ago as 7000 years b.o., and that by the fifth millenium B.C. brewing businesses already existed.It appears, too, that the belief that hops were first used during the eighth to tenth centuries a.d. was erroneous, for the Hebrews are supposed to hnve learned their use in the Babylonian captivity of the eighth and seventh centuries B.C. Whether hops were used in Egypt has not been discovered, but some plant of the Rue family appears to have been used there as a flavouring herb.Ancient Babylonian Seal Cylinder or the Tims or Hamurabi.Dbinkino Beer Through a Tube.The practice of the fermentation industries is based on the ac cumulations of nine milleniums of experience, but the elaboration of explanatory theories is a matter of much more recent growth, 1 "Bier und Bierbereitung bei den VOlkern der Urzeit."Borlin, 1926.
