TY  - JOUR
ID  - SG-0ADF422E938E
TI  - Gut Microbiome, Disease, and Diet: Leveraging Big Data for Precise Nutrition
AU  - Zhiqiang Huang
AU  - Chunming Ye
AU  - Kun Liu
AU  - Wenwen Ma
AU  - Qing Liu
AU  - D Y Li
JO  - Food Science and Human Wellness
PY  - 2026
DO  - 10.26599/fshw.2026.9251155
AB  - Abstract Gut microbiota has profound effects on host health and disease. It is now well acknowledged that diet is a key determinant in shaping gut microbiota. Meanwhile, gut microbiota is an important mediator of the effects of dietary metabolism on the body. Understanding the specific effects and underlying mechanisms of nutrients in diet-microbe-host interactions would support innovation of new intervention strategies to improve health through gut microbiome regulation and nutrient intervention. Advances in multi-omics and artificial intelligence (AI) enable precise gut microbiota modulation and precise nutrition through big data and modeling algorithms. In this context, this review introduces the microenvironment of gut microbiota and its potential mechanisms in diseases. Then, we detail current knowledge regarding how diet modulates gut microbiota and its metabolic activity. Furthermore, we explore how diet can be used as a therapeutic and preventive tool based on big data and AI algorithms. However, causal inference among diet, the gut microbiota, and disease remains limited, and more importantly, the lack of high-quality datasets and standardized analytical frameworks further constrains the clinical translation of precision nutrition strategies. Future research should focus on integrating diverse data with AI-driven modeling to uncover causal diet–microbiome–health relationships, while also building more comprehensive datasets and conducting large-scale, standardized clinical validation. These developments will support the implementation of precision dietary interventions and their translation into real-world applications for personalized disease prevention and health management.
UR  - https://doi.org/10.26599/fshw.2026.9251155
