TI  - Development of multiscale x-ray tomography at SPring-8 BL47XU
AU  - Kentaro Uesugi
AU  - Masahiro Yasutake
AU  - Akihisa Takeuchi
JO  - AIP conference proceedings
PY  - 2023
DO  - 10.1063/5.0168128
AB  - X-ray micro/nano-tomography (multiscale tomography) has been developed at SPring-8 BL47XU. The X-ray optics consists of a simple projection type imaging system and a full-field x-ray microscope using a Fresnel zone plate (FZP) as an objective. There are two objectives with different parameter FZPs, therefore three modes are available in this system. 1. Micro-tomography mode, 2. Large field nano-tomography mode 3. High resolution nano-tomography mode. Furthermore, two types of detectors with different effective pixel sizes can be used in the two nano-tomography modes. All components are mounted on high precision stages driven by stepper motor. It takes about three minutes to change the mode from “micro” to “nano” or “nano” to “nano”. This system enables 3D measurements at several levels of spatial resolution without dismount the sample in the energy range between 7 keV and 15keV.
